+# Agent Note: Backfill incomplete cold projection caches within the list probe bound
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-31-bounded-cold-projection-cache-backfill.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The projection cache could contain valid rows for older client-visible units while missing a unit registered by the current composition or retaining that unit at an incompatible `stateVersion`. Session listing treated a cached `sessionListMetadata.blank: false` row as sufficient and skipped its bounded cold observation, so opening the same Session repeatedly remained the only way to reconstruct the missing client values. The cache was still a valid acceleration, but consumers had no generic signal that its selected client-visible rows were incomplete.
+
+## Decision
+
+The projection registry reports checkpoint completeness against the currently registered client-visible units. A selected row is usable only when its key is present, its `stateVersion` matches, and its stored state and client view pass their schemas. Host-only units do not affect client completeness, and an explicitly empty selection is complete.
+
+`cachedSnapshot` includes this completeness signal with any usable values. Session listing retains its consumer-owned `coldBlankProbeMaxBytes` policy: a missing or incomplete cache makes a physically bounded cold artifact eligible for one exact Session observation. A prepared observation supplies its complete ordered log to `coldSnapshot`, which refolds and schedules a fail-soft write of the complete current checkpoint. The cache never locates or reads Session persistence itself.
+
+A live observation is not written through the cold path because its events may lead the durable log. Artifacts above the bound, location-less sources, vanished files, and failed observations remain visible with their available stale hints. Subagent listing keeps its cache/observation resolution and does not write back because that consumer has no bounded source policy.
+
+## Relationship to existing decisions
+
+This decision preserves the state/client-view split in [Separate session projection state from client views](../architecture/2026-08-19-session-projection-state-and-client-views.md), the persistence-independent cache ownership in [Projection cache as per-session files](../architecture/2026-08-19-projection-cache-per-session-files.md), and the consumer-owned read policies in [Session observations and projection-owned client state](../architecture/2026-08-25-session-observations-and-projection-owned-client-state.md). It extends the bounded fallback from [Bound cold blank-session verification](2026-08-13-bounded-cold-blank-verification.md) to repair incomplete client projection rows without expanding the artifact-size budget.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Treat any cached non-blank metadata as sufficient.** Rejected because a valid row for one unit says nothing about client-visible units registered later or bumped to a new state version.
+
+**Let the cache discover and read Session persistence.** Rejected because it would couple the optional acceleration layer to a source backend and duplicate the source and race policy already owned by SessionQuery and its consumers.
+
+**Refold every incomplete cached Session during listing.** Rejected because list latency and I/O would scale with the complete cold corpus. The existing physical-size bound keeps repair work explicit and conservative.
+
+**Write back every exact observation.** Rejected because other consumers have different work budgets, and a live observation can lead the durable log. The bounded Session-list consumer is the current source of authority for this repair.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Adding or version-bumping a client-visible projection converges cache records when users list eligible small cold Sessions. The refolded values serve the current list immediately while the cache refresh completes asynchronously; a failed refresh logs a warning and leaves the source projection successful. Large or unavailable artifacts can remain incomplete until another durable checkpoint path runs, so their list rows stay visible and may omit newer hints.
+
+Focused registry tests cover missing, mismatched, malformed, selected, and host-only rows. Cache tests cover incomplete detection and asynchronous write-back. Session Controller tests cover an incomplete cached non-blank row entering the bounded observation path while large and failed sources preserve conservative visibility.
